[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds
two problems. Each needs its own fix, and each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 does not close #4471. The booking-v3 form stays broken after it
ships, and the one-day moves need a check of their own.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

This is the desk's own view of #4471, built from the ticket export at render time. Each row is
one problem with its own ticket, and each ticket counts its reports the way this table does:

| row | problem | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the shared parser reads day-first dates month first | <a href="{repo}/1">#1</a> |
| `hint` | the booking-v3 form hints `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads the date day first | <a href="{repo}/2">#2</a> |

The reports in the footnote, read as a one-day move, are filed under `parser` by tenant and count
in #1. Their notes are kept in <a href="{repo}/3">#3</a>, closed as tracked inside #1.

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. The day and the month swap: 2 March becomes 3 February. It reaches every channel
  of every tenant.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, but reads what people
  type the tenant's way, day first. People follow the hint, and the date swaps. Only reports that
  came in through the form, at a tenant on booking-v3. Fixing the parser does not fix this; the
  hint has to match what the form reads.
- **one-day move**, inside `parser`: the booking moves by one day, not by a swap. Tuesday
  becomes Monday, one client gets Tuesday while another in a different time zone gets Monday.
  Check these reports again once the #1 fix ships: a time zone shift would survive it.

## Why one ticket hid two

- Triage merges on the subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  "Wrong date" fits both problems, so both landed in one ticket. Merging on subject
  alone needs a cause check before it.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant: the "tagged as"
  column shows how often it disagrees. Group by tenant, form and channel, as `causes.ts` does.
- The table above already marked `hint` as "no ticket of its own" and footnoted the one-day
  moves. Status `known` made it read as finished.

